  "description": "The PD 1 features our low stand-over height frame for easier climbing in & out of the saddle and affordable specs for an entry level model. Its lightweight full aluminum frame features an internal head tube, internal cable routing and an improved kickstand position. It comes standard with a 3x8 drive train, versatile and capable of handling a wide variety of terrain. It features double-wall rims, stainless spokes and Kenda Kwick Seven.5 tires with reflective sidewalls for increased safety. The PD1 model features a Suntour XCT-28 suspension fork with 100mm of travel for comfort and is your trusted partner for community and outreach patrols.\nHaro PD1 27.5\" X6 frame, internal cable routing\nSuntour XCE-28 fork, 100mm Travel\nShimano FC-TY301 42/34/24T crankset\nShimano Altus RD-310 8-spd rear derailleur\nPivit Adjustable-rise stem, ext.: 105mm\nComfort grips w/ integrated Bar-Ends\nComfort PD1 saddle\nMX-21 27.5\" Aluminum DW rims w/ Stainless spokes\nKenda Kwick Seven 2.2\" tires w/ reflective stripes\nPromax disc brakes w/ 160mm rotors\nRear rack, water-bottle cage & kickstand",
